    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present risk is dominated by two critical paths: untrusted customer email can influence broad CRM reads and irreversible outbound email, and the design uses over-privileged service credentials without structural recipient or authorization binding. The only declared preventive control on exfiltration is a prompt rule, which earns limited residual credit and decays under model upgrades. Forecast remains critical because the strongest present control likely to decay first is ctrl.prompt_no_cross_customer_disclosure, and model upgrades are explicitly allowed without separate review. Manual validation was applied because scripts could not be run."
